Honor GIO_EXTRA_MODULES even when the process looks setuid/secure (OHOS).

On OpenHarmony the WebKit network/web processes are spawned as native child processes via
appspawn. GLib's g_check_setuid() reports these as "secure" (AT_SECURE / capabilities), so
GIO_EXTRA_MODULES is ignored and the glib-networking TLS module (libgioopenssl.so) is never
scanned -> "TLS support is not available" for all https loads. The app points GIO_EXTRA_MODULES
at its own read-only module dir, so honoring it here is safe.
---
diff --git a/gio/giomodule.c b/gio/giomodule.c
index 7311775..0c6fbe2 100644
--- a/gio/giomodule.c
+++ b/gio/giomodule.c
@@ -1335,7 +1335,7 @@ _g_io_modules_ensure_loaded (void)
       scope = g_io_module_scope_new (G_IO_MODULE_SCOPE_BLOCK_DUPLICATES);
 
       /* First load any overrides, extras (but not if running as setuid!) */
-      module_path = !is_setuid ? g_getenv ("GIO_EXTRA_MODULES") : NULL;
+      module_path = g_getenv ("GIO_EXTRA_MODULES");
       if (module_path)
 	{
 	  gchar **paths;
